Explanation of the schedule:

• Morning – You begin at Russian Hill at 09:00. You head to the Presidio (14‑minute travel) to meet William (available 07:00–12:45) from about 09:14 to 10:14 (60 minutes). Then you travel from Presidio to Alamo Square (19 minutes) to meet Kimberly (availability 09:00–14:30) for her required 105 minutes from 10:33 to 12:18.

• Early afternoon – You then leave Alamo Square (12:18) and head to the Financial District (17‑minute ride) arriving about 12:35. After waiting until Joshua’s available start time at 14:30, you meet him (Financial District, 14:30–16:00 for 90 minutes). Immediately after, you make the short 8‑minute trip from Financial District to Nob Hill so you can begin your 120‑minute meeting with Patricia from 16:08 to 18:08 (Patricia’s window is 15:00–19:15).

• Evening – From Nob Hill you travel 27 minutes to the Sunset District arriving at 18:35 so you can have a quick 15‑minute meeting with David (18:35–18:50; his window is very forgiving, 09:15–22:00). Next, you drive 12 minutes from Sunset to Richmond (arriving 19:02) for a brief 15‑minute meeting with Charles (who’s available 17:15–21:00). Then, a 19‑minute ride takes you from Richmond to the Embarcadero, arriving at 19:36 so that you can meet Ronald for 30 minutes (19:36–20:06; his window is 18:15–20:45). Finally, a 10‑minute trip gets you from Embarcadero to Union Square; though you arrive around 20:16 you wait until Kenneth becomes available at 21:15 and meet him for 15 minutes (21:15–21:30).

This plan (often called Option A2) meets the minimum duration requirements for each friend while respecting location‐to‐location travel times and their availability windows – and in doing so you maximize the number of friends you can see (8 out of 10, since the four “conflict‐block” friends in the early afternoon can only yield two meetings given their mutually overlapping windows).
